    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2025/06/puma-fast-r-nitro-elite-3-review-2025.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: Nitro Elite foam gives a soft, bouncy ride, with a softer heel and a soft-but-responsive forefoot that provides strong impact protection at race efforts.",
        "Responsiveness: Energy return is elite, with the foam plus full-length extended carbon plate producing a highly propulsive, snappy toe-off that improves as pace increases.",
        "Stability: Torsional rigidity is very high (minimal flexibility) due to the stiff plate, but heel and midfoot stability are less secure, including noted medial bias; forefoot support is comparatively better.",
        "Durability: Outsole wear is a weakness because the outsole can get permanently indented by rocks/pebbles, and overall durability is described as average."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2025/04/puma-fast-r-nitro-elite-3-review-bold.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The Nitrofoam Elite midsole is described as deeply cushioned, very soft, and bouncy, with excellent forefoot feel and reassuring toe-off, while the split heel feels less stable/reliable at slower paces.",
        "Responsiveness: The ride is highly dynamic and energetic, with explosive rebound, strong rocker-assisted roll, and powerful propulsion/snappy toe-off during hard efforts.",
        "Stability: Forefoot control and toe-off leverage are strong, and the upper/heel lockdown is secure with a rigid heel cup, but overall stability is limited by a soft, narrow split heel that can feel wobbly (especially for heel strikers or when form breaks down).",
        "Durability: The Ultraweave upper is thin but reported as capable and resistant to stretching, PumaGrip outsole quality is viewed positively, and Puma's stated lifespan is about 300 km (200 mi)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Believe in the Run",
      "priority": 5,
      "url": "https://believeintherun.com/shoe-reviews/puma-fast-r-nitro-elite-3-review/",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The Fast-R 3 is described as having a softer ride with a good amount of soft cushioning, and its 40 mm heel / 32 mm forefoot stack indicates substantial impact protection in both heel and forefoot.",
        "Responsiveness: The midsole is repeatedly called bouncier and the shoe extremely fast; workout anecdotes and cited run-economy gains indicate strong energy return and snappy propulsion.",
        "Stability: The carbon plate is lighter and less rigid, and the upper is noted as a bit unstructured, suggesting a less rigid, less locked-down feel with potentially reduced lateral/heel support versus firmer racers.",
        "Durability: Durability evidence is limited in the provided text; it mentions a PUMAGRIP outsole but gives no concrete outsole-wear or long-term material longevity results."
      ]
    }
